 for a deposit before treating you (Republic Act No. 10932).",{"children":"To appropriate and humane care, without discrimination. In an emergency, the ER will not ask for a deposit before treating you (Republic Act No. 10932)."}],["$","li","To be told about your condition, the treatment we recommend, its risks and alternatives, and the expected costs — in Cebuano, Filipino or English.",{"children":"To be told about your condition, the treatment we recommend, its risks and alternatives, and the expected costs — in Cebuano, Filipino or English."}],["$","li","To give or refuse consent before any procedure, and to refuse treatment after its risks are explained.",{"children":"To give or refuse consent before any procedure, and to refuse treatment after its risks are explained."}],["$","li","To privacy and confidentiality. Your records and results are released only to you or someone you authorise in writing.",{"children":"To privacy and confidentiality. Your records and results are released only to you or someone you authorise in writing."}],["$","li","To choose your doctor, and to ask for a second opinion.",{"children":"To choose your doctor, and to ask for a second opinion."}],["$","li","To an itemised bill, with PhilHealth, HMO, senior and PWD benefits applied.",{"children":"To an itemised bill, with PhilHealth, HMO, senior and PWD benefits applied."}],["$","li","To leave the hospital. We will not detain you for an unpaid bill (Republic Act No. 9439); the billing section will arrange a promissory note.",{"children":"To leave the hospital. We will not detain you for an unpaid bill (Republic Act No. 9439); the billing section will arrange a promissory note."}],"$L2c","$L2d","$L2e","$L2f","$L30"]}],"$L31","$L32","$L33","$L34","$L35"],"$L36"]}],"$L37"]}]]
2c:["$","li","To a copy of your medical records, on written request.",{"children":"To a copy of your medical records, on written request."}]
2d:["$","li","To have your religious beliefs respected, and to see a minister of your faith.",{"children":"To have your religious beliefs respected, and to see a minister of your faith."}]
2e:["$","li","To refuse to take part in research.",{"children":"To refuse to take part in research."}]
2f:["$","li","To receive visitors and messages, within the hospital's visiting rules.",{"children":"To receive visitors and messages, within the hospital's visiting rules."}]
30:["$","li","To raise a concern or complaint without it affecting your care.",{"children":"To raise a concern or complaint without it affecting your care."}]
31:["$","h2","2",{"className":"mt-8 mb-3 font-display text-[22px] font-bold text-ink-900 nav:text-[26px]","children":"Your responsibilities"}]
32:["$","ul","3",{"className":"mb-[18px] flex list-disc flex-col gap-2.5 pl-[22px] text-[15.5px] leading-[1.7] text-ink-700 nav:text-base","children":[["$","li","Give complete and accurate information about your health, medicines and allergies.",{"children":"Give complete and accurate information about your health, medicines and allergies."}],["$","li","Follow the treatment plan you agreed to, or tell your doctor if you decide not to.",{"children":"Follow the treatment plan you agreed to, or tell your doctor if you decide not to."}],["$","li","Respect other patients and hospital staff, and follow the visiting rules — one watcher per patient, and no children under 7 in patient rooms.",{"children":"Respect other patients and hospital staff, and follow the visiting rules — one watcher per patient, and no children under 7 in patient rooms."}],["$","li","Bring your PhilHealth, HMO, senior or PWD documents, and settle your bill or make arrangements at the billing section.",{"children":"Bring your PhilHealth, HMO, senior or PWD documents, and settle your bill or make arrangements at the billing section."}],["$","li","Ask questions whenever something is unclear.",{"children":"Ask questions whenever something is unclear."}]]}]
33:["$","h2","4",{"className":"mt-8 mb-3 font-display text-[22px] font-bold text-ink-900 nav:text-[26px]","children":"Raising a concern"}]
34:["$","p","5",{"className":"mb-[18px] text-[15.5px] leading-[1.7] text-ink-700 nav:text-base","children":"Speak first to the nurse in charge of your ward or the admitting desk. You can also send us a message through the Contact page, or call the trunkline at (032) 484 1200. Concerns are reviewed by hospital administration."}]
35:["$","p","6",{"className":"mb-[18px] text-[15.5px] leading-[1.7] text-ink-700 nav:text-base","children":"In an emergency, go straight to the ER or call (032) 484 1234."}]
